/* book: lead: Real gas streams carry several solutes, and one solvent must take them all: each solute has its own equilibrium line, but one L/G serves every component. A reactive solvent goes further: it consumes the dissolved solute, so the liquid holds far more and the absorption rate rises by an enhancement factor. These ideas set solvent choice and column size for amine CO₂ and H₂S removal and lime SO₂ scru */
